#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:2
msgid "LED dimming with PWM"
msgstr "Zatamnjivanje LED diode pomoću PWM-a"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:4
msgid ""
"The :doc:`../analog/analog-output` page used an RC low-pass filter to "
"extract a DC voltage from a PWM signal. For an LED, the filter is not needed"
" -- the human eye itself does the averaging."
msgstr ""
"Stranica :doc:`../analog/analog-output` koristila je RC niskopropusni filtar"
" za izvlačenje istosmjernog napona iz PWM signala. Za LED diodu filtar nije "
"potreban -- usrednjavanje obavlja samo ljudsko oko."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:9
#, python-format
msgid ""
"When an LED is switched on and off faster than about 60 Hz, the visual "
"system stops resolving individual pulses and perceives a steady brightness "
"equal to the average light output. A 50 % duty cycle reads as roughly half "
"brightness; 25 % as a quarter; 10 % as dim."
msgstr ""
"Kada se LED dioda uključuje i isključuje brže od oko 60 Hz, vidni sustav "
"prestaje razlučivati pojedinačne impulse i percipira ujednačenu svjetlinu "
"jednaku prosječnom izlazu svjetlosti. Radni ciklus od 50 % čita se kao "
"otprilike pola svjetline; 25 % kao četvrtina; 10 % kao prigušeno."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:15
msgid ""
"The wiring is the same as for a static external LED on :doc:`../gpio-"
"output/gpio-output` -- a current-limiting resistor in series with the LED, "
"sized using the rules from :doc:`../gpio-output/electronics-basics`. The "
"change is only in software: the pin runs as a :class:`~machine.PWM` output "
"instead of a plain :data:`Pin.OUT <machine.Pin.OUT>`."
msgstr ""
"Ožičenje je isto kao za statičnu vanjsku LED diodu na :doc:`../gpio-"
"output/gpio-output` -- otpornik za ograničavanje struje u seriji s LED "
"diodom, dimenzioniran pomoću pravila iz :doc:`../gpio-output/electronics-"
"basics`\\ . Promjena je samo u softveru: pin radi kao :class:`~machine.PWM` "
"izlaz umjesto običnog :data:`Pin.OUT <machine.Pin.OUT>`\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:23
msgid "Picking the frequency"
msgstr "Odabir frekvencije"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:25
msgid ""
"For LED dimming the PWM frequency only has to clear the eye's flicker "
"threshold:"
msgstr ""
"Za zatamnjivanje LED diode PWM frekvencija mora samo prijeći prag treperenja"
" oka:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:28
msgid "Below ~60 Hz the eye sees the pulses outright."
msgstr "Ispod ~60 Hz oko vidi impulse izravno."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:29
msgid ""
"Below ~200 Hz peripheral vision and rapid eye motion can still reveal "
"flicker."
msgstr ""
"Ispod ~200 Hz periferni vid i brzo kretanje oka još uvijek mogu otkriti "
"treperenje."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:31
msgid "1 kHz is comfortably above all of that and is a typical default."
msgstr "1 kHz je udobno iznad svega toga i tipična je zadana vrijednost."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:34
msgid ""
"There is no upper bound that matters for a small LED on a GPIO; anything "
"from 1 kHz to 10 kHz behaves the same to the eye."
msgstr ""
"Ne postoji gornja granica koja je važna za malu LED diodu na GPIO-u; bilo "
"što od 1 kHz do 10 kHz ponaša se isto za oko."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:38
msgid "Fading"
msgstr "Postupno tamnjenje i posvjetljivanje"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:40
msgid ""
"A fade-in / fade-out loop sweeps the duty cycle from off to fully on and "
"back, dwelling briefly at each step:"
msgstr ""
"Petlja postupnog posvjetljivanja / tamnjenja pomiče radni ciklus od "
"isključenog do potpuno uključenog i natrag, kratko zadržavajući na svakom "
"koraku:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:58
msgid ""
"At 1 kHz PWM and 5 ms steps the eye sees a smooth fade in both directions, "
"with the apparent brightness tracking the duty value."
msgstr ""
"Pri PWM-u od 1 kHz i koracima od 5 ms oko vidi gladak prijelaz u oba smjera,"
" pri čemu prividna svjetlina prati vrijednost radnog ciklusa."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:62
msgid ""
"Perceived brightness is not strictly linear in duty cycle -- the eye's "
"response follows roughly a square or cube law -- so a linear sweep of "
"``duty_u16`` does not look like a linear sweep of brightness. For a "
"perceptually smoother fade, step the duty on a curve."
msgstr ""
"Percipirana svjetlina nije strogo linearna u odnosu na radni ciklus -- odziv"
" oka slijedi otprilike kvadratni ili kubni zakon -- pa linearno pomicanje "
"vrijednosti ``duty_u16`` ne izgleda kao linearno pomicanje svjetline. Za "
"percepcijski glađi prijelaz, mijenjajte radni ciklus po krivulji."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:68
msgid ""
"A convenient integer-only trick is to step an 8-bit counter and use its "
"square as the duty cycle. ``255 × 255 = 65025`` is within rounding of full "
"scale, so the sweep covers the whole range:"
msgstr ""
"Praktičan trik samo s cijelim brojevima jest mijenjati 8-bitni brojač i "
"koristiti njegov kvadrat kao radni ciklus. ``255 × 255 = 65025`` je unutar "
"zaokruživanja pune skale, pa raspon pokriva cijelo područje:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/pwm/led-dimming.rst:88
msgid ""
"The fade now feels roughly even in apparent brightness from off to full."
msgstr ""
"Prijelaz se sada osjeća približno ujednačen po prividnoj svjetlini od "
"isključenog do punog."
